-- title:
--   Evaluated Slice Commutation Q SDDOp Avg Eq
-- statement:
--   **Averaged evaluated-slice squared distance in scalar form.** Let $S$ be a symmetric projective strategy for $(m+1,q,d)$ and let $G^x$ be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family for $(m,q,d)$. Let $\mathcal D$ be the uniform distribution on evaluated-slice questions, and let $\mathsf L$ and $\mathsf R$ be the left and reversed right raw product families. Let $s_2(q)$ and $s_4(q)$ be the `ABA` and `ABAB` outcome sums from the preceding swap identity. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{sddErrorOp}(\psi,\mathcal D,\mathsf L,\mathsf R)=2\left(\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}s_2(q)-\mathbb E_{q\sim\mathcal D}s_4(q)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This exact expansion is the bridge from the operator-valued evaluated-slice distance to the scalar commutativity estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.evaluatedSliceCommutation_qSDDOp_avg_eq`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/EvaluatedSliceCommutation/Averages.lean#L206-L324

